==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|it|replica}}, derived from {{der|en|la|replico|replicare|to fold or bend back; to reply}}. Doublet of {{m|en|reply}} and {{m|en|replicate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛplɪkə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-replica.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|repliche<l:rare>}}

# An exact [[copy]].
#: {{ux|en|The statue on the museum floor is an authentic '''replica'''.}}
# A [[copy]] made at a smaller [[scale]] than the [[original]].
#: {{cot|en|scale model}}
#: {{ux|en|He collected '''replicas''' of old cars.}}

